From 95e09c05a008cd4269c02e35de623d3ad7d82fc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CustomKIMI <customkimi@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:12:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] customkimi: retry automatically when Gemini's filter
 blocks a reply

When a reply is Gemini's block notice ("This request was blocked by
Gemini's filters ...") or a request fails with it, the agent sends a
random spintax "continue" prompt and keeps going inside the same turn,
up to 5 times in a row; then it stops with a warning. On a Gemini model
a reply cut off by the provider's filter (finishReason=filtered) counts
too. Every retry shows a warning line with the prompt it sent.

It runs in the main agent and in subagents. A subagent retries inside
its own run, so the parent receives the real answer. The new top-level
setting gemini_filter_retry chooses who retries: true (all agents, the
default), "subagents" (subagents only) or false (off). /settings has a
"Gemini filter retry" entry with On / Subagents only / Off.

A blocked reply is continued with a turn-scoped loop nudge from the
onDidFinishStep hook. A failed request goes through a new
IAgentLoopService.registerLlmRecovery seam: the turn machine's recovery
proposal re-runs the step, and the loop appends the continue message to
context after closing the failed step, since v2 builds requests from
context memory. A live nudge now also keeps a filtered step from
failing the turn, and turn.filtered follows the last step.
